# Contact form delivery
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in the values, then set
# the SAME variables in the hosting dashboard — Vercel/Netlify build from the
# repo, and never see your local .env.
#
# The form works without these: it validates, then hands the visitor a prefilled
# email to support@convexfunding.com instead of pretending to have sent
# something. Set them to have it actually deliver.

# Where the form POSTs its JSON. Any relay that accepts a JSON body works.
#   Web3Forms   https://api.web3forms.com/submit      (needs the access key below)
#   Formspree   https://formspree.io/f/<your-form-id> (no access key needed)
#   Your own    /api/contact                          (a serverless function)
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=

# Only for relays that want a key in the body, e.g. Web3Forms. Leave blank otherwise.
#
# IMPORTANT: anything with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the JavaScript bundle
# and is therefore PUBLIC — readable by anyone who opens devtools. A form-relay
# access key is designed for that and is safe here.
#
# A mail-provider API key (SendGrid, Resend, Mailgun, SMTP credentials) is NOT,
# and must never go in this file. Those belong in a serverless function's own
# environment, with VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT pointing at that function.
VITE_CONTACT_ACCESS_KEY=
